      "summary": ": Today's Ski Summary 13 August 2026 — 12:40 PM NZ time: Cardrona Alpine Resort is OPEN today, with a mainly fine day ahead and some high cloud. The groomers have been out laying down fresh corduroy, setting up the mountain for some great turns. There are several activities taking place on the mountain today, including school skiing with Wānaka Primary, film shoots and race training. Main Basin lifts are scheduled from 8:30 AM, with Captains, T-Bar, Soho and Willows scheduled to follow from 9:00 AM. Big Willows and Summit are delayed. The resort has not provided a specific opening time for either in the current report. Wells Pipe Platter is closed. The resort is also reminding guests to take care on the access road as thawing conditions have made some sections muddy. The road is currently chain-free, but chains must still be carried due to the active road hazard advisory. Cardrona also has several important guest announcements today: season-pass holders need to have a photo on their profile/pass this year, while the resort is hosting Wānaka Primary School, film shoots and race training on the mountain.",
